 },
 "protocol": "VERA v6 analysis: one small, pre-registered set of models.\n\nFixed before any v6 number was seen:\n  * Labels: list-aware negation (v5 parser negated only the first item of \"no X, Y, or Z\"), CheXpert\n    hierarchy (opacity <- consolidation / pneumonia / ...), and two label sets:\n      strict (PRIMARY): 1 = the reference contradicts the claim, 0 = supported, unmentioned = excluded\n      broad: 1 = contradicted or unmentioned, 0 = supported (the v2-v5 definition, now with fixed parsing)\n  * Claims evaluated: positive, un-hedged abnormal claims of the GREEDY report.\n  * Protocol (PRIMARY): 5-fold cross-validation grouped by image over all images; every model is fit on\n    the training folds only (C chosen by inner grouped CV); out-of-fold scores are pooled. 95% CIs and\n    paired tests by image bootstrap. Secondary: train on the calibration split, test on the test split.\n  * Headline model: \"VERA (full, model-internal)\". No selection among candidates.\nFeature families (nothing from the reference is ever a feature):\n  A  finding-word attention per layer x head: image share, share relative to the report, attention on the\n     named region (raw, area-normalised lift, contrast vs the report), computed online for every report\n  T  text the model wrote; C token confidence at the finding word\n  S  self-consistency: does the finding come back in 3 sampled reports of the same image?\n  Q  self-verification: the model's own P(yes) to \"Does this chest X-ray show <finding>?\"\n  V  external classifier (torchxrayvision, not trained on IU); I image-level attention (control)\n"
}